# CODE. Four existing files changed on 2026-09-19 and two are new. Change log, most recent first:
#
#   code/zerod_ffr.py       -> 9f3ffb20...   TWO changes, both verified against the full suite.
#       (i) DECISION B3: new `trunc_ref` parameter pins the modelled node set, by coordinate, to a reference tree,
#       and the reference is AUTHORITATIVE (assignment, not intersection). A calibre-only error must not change
#       WHICH vessels are modelled; a fixed truncation radius was deleting 489 of 655 discrete outlets cohort-wide
#       under T4, with 56 of 148 trees losing their bed entirely.
#       (ii) Viscosity `mu` became an instance attribute defaulting to the module constant — needed because the
#       negative class must vary haematocrit and a module constant cannot be varied per draw. Default behaviour is
#       identical. Verified after both: self-test unchanged, V1-V10 PASS on BOTH beds (scans 14, 306), and the
#       ablation smoke is BIT-IDENTICAL (max numeric difference 0 across all 45 columns).
#
#   code/ablation.py        -> e0ca8325...   DETECTOR RECORDING COLUMNS (additive), on top of the minimiser fix and
#       decisions B1/B3 earlier the same day. run_id on every row; C_abs (the detector may use only the ABSOLUTE
#       tuned parameter, never C_ratio, which needs a clean model it would not have); the S_C covariates from the
#       CORRUPTED model; a CLEAN row per (instance, bed); and two long-format side files keyed by run_id.
#       protocol_c_targets() returns TRIPLES so a territory's clean subtree travels with its own target.
#       THE EXPERIMENT DID NOT MOVE: every corrupted row bit-identical to the pre-change run.
#       Earlier the same day: Protocol C's minimiser was a local method on a BIMODAL loss and returned the wrong
#       basin on a real instance (dFFR -0.52 against a true ~0) — a false absorption count and a false H5 positive;
#       and B1 changed Protocol C's target to the clean tree's FULL territory outflow, partitioned by the CLEAN
#       tree's territories.
#
#   code/error_types.py     -> 8401c915...   DECISION B2 plus a header correction. T2_KEEP_BEYOND 15e-3 -> 25e-3:
#       it was SHORTER than RUNOFF (20 mm), so T2's truncation deleted the measurement node its own docstring said
#       it preserved (meas_same_point False in 36/36 T2 smoke rows). The guard now lives beside the constant and is
#       a RAISE, not an assert — `python -O` strips asserts. T3_LENGTH_DELTA and T4_RADIUS_SCALE are UNCHANGED.
#
#   code/export_cfd_case.py -> d49a2c32...   CFD case packages, per CFD-ARM-SPEC §11, after two rounds of
#       independent review (MUST 1-8, then two DO-NOT-SEND items). Among them: a §13 blinding violation, a mask
#       deletion rule that eroded the retained vessel by ~1300 voxels, and inlet normals 37 degrees off.
#
#   code/negatives.py       -> f57042d1...   NEW. The detector's negative class (DETECTOR-SPEC §5): correct anatomy
#       tuned against a noisy measurement. Verified non-degenerate (residual median 0.072, not ~1e-9). Physiological
#       SDs cited 2026-09-19 and all three moved, by factors of 2 to 8 — the placeholders had been population and
#       inter-instrument figures where within-subject was required. SD_TERRITORY_SHARE remains UNCITED and is the
#       most load-bearing constant in the file.
#
#   code/ingest_cfd_radius.py -> 5e2b1358...   NEW. Rebuilds the 0D twin from the as-meshed radius the CFD side
#       returns, inheriting the healthy reference and bed from the package's tree so only the epicardial radius
#       differs. Not yet exercised on real returned data — only on a synthetic return.
#
#   2026-09-19 (late): COMMENT-ONLY on both files, no constant moved. zerod_ffr.py -- MURRAY_EXP = 2.66 flagged as
#       uncited and outside the pooled empirical exponent 2.39 (CI 2.24-2.54, Taylor 2024); NOT changed, because it
#       feeds the discrete eligibility gate and hence the frozen 3D subset. negatives.py -- SD_TERRITORY_SHARE
#       citation-searched (no single value supportable; sensitivity band added) and WSCV_TARGET flagged as ~half
#       Kaufmann 1999's regional figure. Both noise terms err toward an EASY negative class, so the detector's
#       specificity is declared an upper bound.
#       CORRECTION, same day: the MURRAY_EXP flag was WITHDRAWN. 2.66 is 8/3, the MASS-diameter exponent of
#       Choy & Kassab 2008 (M ~ A^(4/3), A ~ D^2), and it allocates myocardial bed to an outlet. Taylor 2024's 2.39
#       pools the FLOW-diameter exponent -- a different quantity, so it was never evidence against this one. The
#       constant is cited, not chosen. Measured effect of using 2.39 instead: median 0.33 pp of flow share.
#
# Re-verify all of these at registration; if any differs, re-run --verify before trusting a result.
