# NOTE — THERE IS NO VERSION CONTROL ON THIS PROJECT, and that is a real gap for a study that promises a code deposit
# and reproducible figures. This manifest records WHAT changed and WHY, but it cannot show a diff, cannot restore a
# previous state, and every entry above was written by hand. Two workable fixes, neither urgent enough to do
# mid-registration: keep a git repository OUTSIDE the Google Drive tree and sync into it (Drive and .git interact
# badly — Drive can corrupt object files mid-write), or treat the Zenodo deposit as the versioning mechanism and
# deposit on every material change. Decide before the paper claims reproducibility.
